file other.md
# Other doc

Linked from doc.md.
end
file notes.txt
plain text notes
end
run doc.md
wait # Split preview
snap source A markdown file open in the editor, no preview yet.
key ctrl+p
type toggle split
wait Markdown: Toggle Split
snap toggle-split-palette The palette finds Markdown: Toggle Split.
key enter
wait Jump to the other doc
snap split-on The rendered preview opens in a split to the right of the source.
key down*7 alt+right
type  Live.
wait and italic words. Live.
snap live Text typed in the source shows up in the preview right away.
key down*30
wait 37/89
snap cursor-sync Moving the cursor down scrolls the preview to the same section.
wheel 20 10 down 3
wait 49 Paragraph 7
snap editor-wheel Wheeling the editor scrolls the preview along with it.
wheel 90 10 down 3
wait 56 Paragraph 8
snap preview-wheel Wheeling the preview scrolls the editor along with it.
click 90 20
key down*4
wait 61 ## Section 9
snap preview-keys After a click in the preview, arrow keys scroll it and the editor follows.
key esc
type !
wait • item 5a!
snap esc-back-to-editor Esc returns focus to the editor: the typed ! lands in the source and the preview.
wheel 90 10 up 30
wait the other doc
click 70 3
wait Linked from doc.md
snap link Clicking a link in the preview opens the linked markdown file.
key alt+,
wait Jump to the other doc
snap back Alt+, goes back to the previous document.
click 88 3
wait plain text notes
snap plain-buffer A link to a plain text file opens it without a preview split.
key alt+,
wait • item 3a
snap markdown-again Going back to the markdown file brings the split back.
config
{"plugins": {"markdown": {"split_width": 25}}}
end
wait-gone Paragraph 4 has bold and italic words.
snap width-hot-reload Changing split_width in the config resizes the preview without a restart.
key alt+p
wait click a link to open it
snap overlay-over-split Alt+p opens the full preview overlay on top of the split.
key pgdn
wait-gone Section 4
snap overlay-scrolled PgDn scrolls the overlay.
key esc
wait-gone click a link to open it
snap overlay-closed-split-follows Esc closes the overlay and the split is still there.
key alt+o
type notes.txt
wait notes.txt
key enter
wait plain text notes
key ctrl+p
type toggle split
key enter
key alt+,
wait Paragraph
snap toggled-off-from-plain Toggle Split run from a plain buffer turns the split off for the markdown file too.
